@ Index:   Iterative factorial using DSE
@ Tested:  5 returns 120, 0 returns 1, 10 returns 3628800.
@ Input:   X = 5 (also 0 and 10)
@ Output:  X = 120 (0 returns 1, 10 returns 3628800)
@ Author:  Warren Young, assisted by Cursor and Didier Lachieze
@ Created: 2026-10-01
@ Version: 1.0
@
@ Usage is the same as the built-in 𝑥! operation: input value in X,
@ factorial of same output in X; stack-neutral.  Takes any X that
@ the IP op can turn into an integer, but rejects negative.
@
@ As a bonus, this demonstrates several uncommonly-seen ops:
@
@ - FINISH for exiting early upon a detected error condition, with a diagnostic message
@ - DROPy to keep the stack clean; much less common than X-only DROP
@ - program flow via BACK and SKIP
LBL ‘FactIt’
  IP
  𝑥<? 0.            ; factorial is undefined for negative inputs
    FINISH ‘Invalid argument!’
  1.
  𝑥>? Y             ; with passed X (now Y) clamped to integer and ≥ 0…
    SKIP 003        ; …it has to be = 0 here, so clean up and exit
  RCL× Y            ; multiply accumulated X by next Y value
  DSE Y             ; decrement Y (passed as X) until = 0
    BACK 002        ; return to the multiply step
  DROP𝑦             ; passed X now consumed; clean its remnant
  RTN
  END
.END.
